WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back to the show, Al.
How are you?

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm doing great.
How are you doing?

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm doing well.
I can't help but start

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:09.476
by mentioning the fact that when
you were on the show in November

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:12.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the studio, it was
the middle of impeachment,

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:15.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you were saying
it was as dangerous a time

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.583 size:84% position:42% line:92%
as we've lived through,

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
and yet it seems
incredibly quaint now.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
This does seem to be a pattern
that every time

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
we think that things
are really bad,

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:27.093
they unfortunately get worse
How are you feeling right now?

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Well, yeah.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.566 line:92%
It's a scary time in many ways

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
because everybody,
whether you're a Republica

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
or Democratic or Independent
or something else --

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
just about every single grou
is feeling

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there's nobody
really in charge,

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:52.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
or at least not in charge
in a positive way.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:56.523
And back when we talked before
that's exactly the time period

00:00:56.523 --> 00:01:00.927
when the country should have
been moving full speed ahead

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:04.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make preparations
for the pandemic

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
about which we had
already been warned.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:12.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You weren't necessarily warne
during the Clinton-Gore

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
administration,
but you were prepared.

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:18.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, I've read that
President Clinton

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
had read a book
about biological warfare

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.015 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and took it seriously,

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you did begin
stockpiling medicine.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did begin
stockpiling vaccines.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
How hard is it to watch
an administration

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:34.160 size:84% position:42%
that does not take this
seriously as a threat?

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, it's hard.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course, it's much harde
to watch and listen

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the families
that have gone through

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.772
such horrific experiences,
and I won't recap them here.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:49.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've all been
going through that,

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
vicariously, for most,
thankfully.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.783 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But it's hard. Yes.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.918 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, um, you know,

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's connected to climate
in this sense.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:06.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
The scientists who warned us
about the pandemic

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
included the very best
epidemiologists and virologist

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the world,
and they warned us

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:15.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
to prepare for a pandemic
that was almost exactly like

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:18.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
the one that
we're struggling with now.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when we hear
the climate scientists

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
arguing for even longer
that we need to do

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
something to stop
the onrushing climate crisis

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:33.720
the lesson seems clearly tha
it's best to listen to them.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
One other thing
they have in common --

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:40.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
both the COVID-19 pandemic
and the climate crisis

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
hit the communities of color
and the poorest Americans

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.967 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
first and hardest

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:52.338 size:84% position:42%
and, in that process,
reveal the really stark

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:56.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
and incredible inequities
and injustices

00:02:56.042 --> 00:03:00.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have been allowed to go o
for way, way too long.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.048 line:92%
We got to do something about it.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.017
-Certainly in parts of the
United States and worldwide,

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:07.353
it does seem like government
are taking this very seriously

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
It does seem like
we are mobilizing

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.958 size:88% position:44% line:92%
against police brutality

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:15.061 size:81% position:41%
in a way that we maybe
haven't ever before.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.462 line:92%
Does that give you confidenc

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we can do the same
for climate?

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.600 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I really believe, Seth,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:26.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we are witnessing
a kind of general awakening.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think
these things compete.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:32.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think it's, you know
a zero-sum situation,

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the more attention
paid to the pandemic,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.284 size:84% position:42%
the less attention paid
to these other things.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:41.054 size:78% position:39%
I think, for example,
about the gains made

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:46.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the LGBTQ community
over the last decade or so

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those gains are not going away
They're being consolidated

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:53.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just had a significant
Supreme Court victory

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
consolidating them.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gender equity gains
of the last several years,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.606 line:92%
they're being consolidated

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:04.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that this awakenin
has touched people

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.312 line:92%
in cities all around the world

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
after the heinous
George Floyd murder.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:13.920 line:92%
It was such a horrible event

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.055 line:92%
and such a cue for people

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
to take off whatever blinder
they had on

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:24.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see and understand
the incredible injustice

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we have allowed to persis
for so long.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:30.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, by the way,
the burning of fossil fuels,

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:34.507
which creates the global-warming
pollution mainly,

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.743 line:92%
also creates the air pollution

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:40.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
that elevates the death rate
under COVID-19.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.782 line:92%
There have been multiple studies

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
showing that communities
and counties

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have more air pollution
from burning fossil fuels

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:53.493
have a significantly highe
death rate from the pandemic

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's true in other countries
as well.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:05:02.168
So we need to -- we need to pu
the Black Lives Matter agend

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:04.537 line:92%
in the center of the plans

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
now being developed
for a green recovery.

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.709 line:92%
We need a just transition

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that those who are likely
to suffer economically

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:17.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
if we don't provide them
with better jobs

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:20.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
in this transition
are taken care of.

